# Component Development Guidelines

## shadcn/ui Components
This project uses shadcn/ui component library. Always use existing components from [src/components/ui/](mdc:src/components/ui/) when possible.

### Available Components
- **Button**: [src/components/ui/button.tsx](mdc:src/components/ui/button.tsx)
- **Card**: [src/components/ui/card.tsx](mdc:src/components/ui/card.tsx)
- **Avatar**: [src/components/ui/avatar.tsx](mdc:src/components/ui/avatar.tsx)
- **Badge**: [src/components/ui/badge.tsx](mdc:src/components/ui/badge.tsx)
- **Accordion**: [src/components/ui/accordion.tsx](mdc:src/components/ui/accordion.tsx)

## Component Patterns

### Styling
- Use Tailwind CSS classes
- Follow the design system established in [src/app/globals.css](mdc:src/app/globals.css)
- Use the `cn()` utility from [src/lib/utils.ts](mdc:src/lib/utils.ts) for conditional classes
- Maintain consistent spacing and color schemes

### Props and Types
- Always define proper TypeScript interfaces
- Use React.ComponentProps for extending HTML element props
- Include proper default values
- Document complex props with JSDoc comments

### Accessibility
- Include proper ARIA attributes
- Use semantic HTML elements
- Ensure keyboard navigation works
- Add focus management where needed
- Include screen reader friendly content

## Design System

### Colors
- **Primary**: Orange (#f97316) and Red (#ef4444) gradients
- **Background**: Orange-50 to Blue-50 gradients
- **Text**: Slate-900 for headings, Slate-600/700 for body text
- **Borders**: Slate-200 for subtle borders

### Spacing
- Use consistent spacing scale (4, 6, 8, 12, 16, 20, 24, etc.)
- Maintain proper padding and margins
- Use responsive spacing (sm:, md:, lg: prefixes)

### Typography
- **Headings**: Bold, proper hierarchy
- **Body text**: Readable line heights
- **Fonts**: Geist Sans for UI, Geist Mono for code

